 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "A gerund is the -ing form of a verb used as a noun: “Singing is fun.”\nA gerund can be:\n• the subject: “Learning a language takes time.”\n• the object after some verbs: enjoy, like, love, hate, finish, stop, avoid, keep, practise, mind: “She enjoys dancing.” “Stop talking!”\n• after a preposition: “He is good at drumming.” “Thank you for helping me.” “I am interested in learning Duala.”\nSpelling: dance → dancing (drop e); swim → swimming (double the consonant); play → playing.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {},
  "problem": "Complete with a gerund: “My sister enjoys ___ (sing) in the choir.”",
  "steps": [
   "After “enjoy” we use a gerund (-ing form).",
   "sing → singing."
  ],
  "answer": "singing",
  "checks": []
 },
